// concepts.memql -- the referencepack reference pack (examples/referencepack).
//
// This file is the schema half of the minimal reference pack that
// demonstrates the memQL pack model end-to-end (epic 2, issue 2.5). It
// declares ONE concept so the pack contributes a real, queryable schema
// to the engine's concept registry the same way a core domain does.
//
// Authorization (owned tier): ownerUserId is the per-row authz key, the
// same pattern every owned core concept uses -- a read path filters on
// payload.ownerUserId == actor.userId, a write path stamps it from
// actor.userId. The field is here so the pack demonstrates an authz-sane
// concept, not just an empty schema.

@version("1.0.0")
@namespace("referencepack")
@description("A minimal greeting record contributed by the reference pack (examples/referencepack). Demonstrates that a pack's embedded .memql concept lands in the engine's concept registry alongside the core domains.")
@displayCard(primary="message", secondary="ownerUserId", tertiary="createdAt")
concept greeting {
  ownerUserId  string  @required  @description("v1:identity:user.id of the owner. Per-row authz key (owned tier); stamped from actor.userId by the writing mutation.")
  message      string  @required  @description("The greeting text, e.g. \"hello from the reference pack\".")
}
